Say where the focus goes after Ctrl+T, and where the next key lands.

Ctrl+T in Chromium's own UI opens a tab whose address bar will not take
typing. Focusing it straight away did nothing visible, and neither did
focusing it one turn of the loop later. Both attempts assumed something
takes the focus back afterwards, and nothing has shown that. The keys do
reach the engine -- the shell sees them land on the web component -- but
which view they reach from there is unknown.

Three places, each answering one part:

- SetFocusToLocationBar: whether it returns before it focuses anything
  (window inactive, location bar hidden), what the tab is loading at that
  moment (chrome://newtab/ as typed or the rewritten chrome://new-tab-page/,
  which also bears on the "chrome://newtab/ for incorrect profile" error),
  and which view holds the focus when it has finished.
- FocusManager::SetFocusedViewWithReason: every change of focused view,
  including the ones only stored because the widget is inactive. If
  something takes the focus back, it shows up here.
- FocusManagerEventHandler::OnKeyEvent: for each key press, the aura
  window it was dispatched to and the view Views thinks is focused. These
  disagree when the page's window holds the aura focus under a toolbar
  view Views thinks is focused.

No key codes and no full URLs are logged -- scheme and host only.

Diagnostic only, and it comes out again once it has answered.

Generated for Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch,
ohos-browser-chrome-shell.patch and ohos-shell-accelerators.patch.

